# NOTE: git does not support trailing comments on a pattern line. `dist/ # foo`
# is one literal pattern that matches nothing, so every comment gets its own line.

# Generated copies of the game. Both are rebuilt by a script, and a second copy
# in git is a copy that will drift.
# dist/      <- tools/build-web.js
# mobile/www <- mobile/sync-web.js
dist/
mobile/www/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Generated native projects (Capacitor recreates them on the build runner)
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The commercial notes stay on disk. The repository is public so that GitHub
# Pages can serve the game for free and the iOS build can use a free macOS
# runner — not to publish the business thinking. The game's own code is readable
# in devtools on the live site either way, so nothing is gained by hiding that;
# these two are different in kind.
#   LAUNCH.md        the ads decision and its reasoning, revenue argument
#   STORE_LISTING.md the store copy, in four languages, before it is submitted
docs/LAUNCH.md
docs/STORE_LISTING.md

# A private key in the clear. Never committed, and the script says to delete it.
signing-out/

# App Review screen recordings and the frames pulled out of them. These are
# recordings of a real phone, and this repository is public.
review/
